<title>UK: FEK sets 10 bln yen three-year dual currency bond.</title>
<headline>FEK sets 10 bln yen three-year dual currency bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced</p>
<p>by joint lead managers New Japan Securities Europe Ltd and Sanwa</p>
<p>International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   FINNISH EXPORT CREDIT</p>
<p> AMT    10 BLN YEN    COUPON     5.34	MATURITY  **17.APR.00</p>
<p> TYPE   DUAL CURRENCY ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    17.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.50	MOODY	AA1	 S&amp;P	   AA</p>
<p> LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ   SEMI-ANN  DENOMS (K)  500</p>
<p>SALE LIMIT US/UK/JAPAN</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.50	SELL CONC  1.00	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES   **REDEMPTION IN U.S DOLLARS AT $4078.30 PER 500,000 YEN</p>
<p>	     ISSURD OFF AN EMTN PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
